      "cues": [
        {
          "id": "patterns",
          "label": "patterns",
          "startSec": 37.65,
          "endSec": 69.1,
          "text": "This pattern repeats everywhere humans have built powerful, autonomous systems. Aviation scaled autonomy by adding checklists, hard limits, and layered safety. Medicine made protocols standard because expertise alone isn't enough under pressure. Organizations delegate power safely by creating budgets, approvals, audits, and reviews. The more powerful the actor, the more critical the guardrails. AI isn't special — it's just newer.",
