          "startSec": 92.85000000000001,
          "endSec": 119.25000000000001,
          "text": "The best teams already add guardrails in Python: schemas, validation, retries, approval gates, sandboxing, and secrets hygiene. The problem isn't that people don't know guardrails matter. The problem is that when you assemble everything by convention across mismatched systems, it's easy to miss a layer. Missing a layer won't feel like a mistake until it becomes an incident.",
