    {
      "id": "sandboxing-a-secretless-broker-boundary",
      "title": "Sandboxing + a Secretless Broker Boundary",
      "startSec": 226.49999999999997,
      "endSec": 280.7,
      "layers": [
        {
          "id": "background",
          "zIndex": -1,
          "components": [
            {
              "id": "background-0",
              "type": "Background",
              "props": {
                "color": "#fdfdfd",
                "sceneStartSec": 222.99999999999997
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "title",
          "zIndex": 1,
          "components": [
            {
              "id": "title-0",
              "type": "Title",
              "props": {
                "text": "Keep the monkey in the box",
                "x": 960,
                "y": 180,
                "textAlign": "center",
                "sceneStartSec": 222.99999999999997
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "subtitle",
          "zIndex": 1,
          "components": [
            {
              "id": "text-block-0",
              "type": "TextBlock",
              "props": {
                "text": "Sandbox untrusted orchestration. Keep secrets out of the runtime. Broker privileged calls behind a narrow, auditable boundary.",
                "x": 960,
                "y": 300,
                "size": 32,
                "align": "center",
                "maxWidth": 1500,
                "font": "serif",
                "sceneStartSec": 222.99999999999997
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "diagram",
          "zIndex": 0,
          "components": [
            {
              "id": "container-sandbox-diagram-0",
              "type": "ContainerSandboxDiagram",
              "props": {
                "containerWidth": 1600,
                "containerHeight": 650,
                "x": 960,
                "y": 690,
                "sceneStartSec": 222.99999999999997
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": "sandbox_broker",
          "label": "sandbox_broker",
          "startSec": 226.49999999999997,
          "endSec": 280.7,
          "text": "Once you let an agent write files or run code, you want a cage. Tactus runs orchestration inside a sandboxed Lua environment, and when sandboxing is enabled, inside an ephemeral container. But containers answer only one security question: what can it touch? The other question is: what can it steal? The broker boundary is the game changer. Keep the runtime secretless and networkless by default. The sandbox can request tool calls, but it never holds provider keys. The keys live outside the sandbox, in a trusted broker. This is the security model: don't make secrets hard to steal—make sure there are no secrets inside the runtime to steal. It's like letting a burglar into an empty building. Even if they get in, there's nothing valuable to take.",
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "tts",
              "startSec": 226.49999999999997,
              "endSec": 239.99999999999997,
              "text": "Once you let an agent write files or run code, you want a cage. Tactus runs orchestration inside a sandboxed Lua environment, and when sandboxing is enabled, inside an ephemeral container."
            },
            {
              "type": "pause",
              "startSec": 239.99999999999997,
              "endSec": 240.49999999999997,
              "durationSec": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "tts",
              "startSec": 240.49999999999997,
              "endSec": 249.14999999999998,
              "text": "But containers answer only one security question: what can it touch? The other question is: what can it steal?"
            },
            {
              "type": "pause",
              "startSec": 249.14999999999998,
              "endSec": 249.64999999999998,
              "durationSec": 0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "tts",
              "startSec": 249.64999999999998,
              "endSec": 265.75,
              "text": "The broker boundary is the game changer. Keep the runtime secretless and networkless by default. The sandbox can request tool calls, but it never holds provider keys. The keys live outside the sandbox, in a trusted broker."
            },
            {
              "type": "pause",
              "startSec": 265.75,
              "endSec": 266.2,
              "durationSec": 0.45
            },
            {
              "type": "tts",
              "startSec": 266.2,
              "endSec": 280.7,
              "text": "This is the security model: don't make secrets hard to steal—make sure there are no secrets inside the runtime to steal. It's like letting a burglar into an empty building. Even if they get in, there's nothing valuable to take."
            }
          ],
          "bullets": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a-concrete-example",
      "title": "A Concrete Example",
      "startSec": 281.2,
      "endSec": 308.19999999999993,
      "layers": [
